+# Q3 revenue drop
+
+East had the steepest fall in revenue from Q2 to Q3 of any region. It went from 333,747.57 to 234,325.08, a drop of 29.8% (−99,422.49). North was next at −4.3%. Ledger Pro accounts for most of East's drop: its revenue fell from 106,520.77 to 23,015.24 (−83,505.53), which is about 84% of the region's total decline. Ledger Pro's transaction count in East went from about 100–120 a month to under 30 in July, August and September, then came back to 100 in October. Revenue is units × unit_price over completed rows only. Refunds (negative units) are netted in, and pending and cancelled rows are left out. Q4 is not a finished quarter: it includes 8,292 rows dated after 18 October 2026.
+
+| Quarter | East revenue |
+|---------|-------------:|
+| Q1      |   333,565.48 |
+| Q2      |   333,747.57 |
+| Q3      |   234,325.08 |
+| Q4      |   305,168.76 |
